<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Okinawa Prefecture</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1879">1879</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Okinawa Prefecture is the southernmost prefecture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, created in 1879 when the Meiji government annexed the Ryukyu Kingdom, deposed King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sho-tai">Sho Tai</a> and abolished the Ryukyu Domain. The islands saw the bloody <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-okinawa">Battle of Okinawa</a> in 1945 and remained under US administration until their return to Japan in 1972. American military bases still occupy much of the main island.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/okinawa-prefecture.jpg" alt="Okinawa Prefecture" width="320" height="186" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CEphoto, Uwe Aranas · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Naha_Okinawa_Japan_Shuri-Castle-01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
